                                        "entry_id": "10082382-914a-351d-93d3-6d45d71586d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crest:",
                                            "A crest (of metal, leather, etc) on a piece of armor, especially on a helmet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d5e3087-15fc-494d-ab96-0bb94179c0fa",
                                                "sense_id": "21052872-2cd3-39be-8112-379e6cde38b6",
                                                "text": "The head-dress of the Horse Grenadiers consists of a peculiar leather helmet with a comb of bear's skin passing over it from ear to ear and a long scarlet […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b981a2e-5338-41ec-a2c4-59ae2abf30d1",
                                                "sense_id": "21052872-2cd3-39be-8112-379e6cde38b6",
                                                "text": "The armet has usually a low central cabled comb with parallel flutes on either side, occasionally there are three or five combs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a70ce7c0-4d2e-4b25-a40a-a9d7d1900344",
                                                "sense_id": "21052872-2cd3-39be-8112-379e6cde38b6",
                                                "text": "The combs or elbow pieces are beautifully made, and over the right armpit is […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30e6e28f-3cd9-47d3-b109-c216dac97fef",
                                                "sense_id": "21052872-2cd3-39be-8112-379e6cde38b6",
                                                "text": "Charles I. (Edinburgh Castle) The Pikeman of the time of James I. was accoutred in a morion-shaped helmet with a comb of moderate size and a flat brim, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45431099-6b40-33aa-a418-57f0ad1d8cf2",
                                        "entry_id": "10082382-914a-351d-93d3-6d45d71586d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A crest:",
                                            "The top part of a gun’s stock."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3240639e-3731-38b1-a68e-c3eacbe72087",
                                        "entry_id": "10082382-914a-351d-93d3-6d45d71586d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A structure of hexagon cells made by bees for storing honey; honeycomb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b053b070-3195-4ece-a674-d8581d49c56f",
                                                "sense_id": "3240639e-3731-38b1-a68e-c3eacbe72087",
                                                "text": "The combs of the wild bees are found on overhanging precipices, and the only means by which they can be reached is to descend from above on narrow cane ladders just wide enough for a man’s foot, and often 300 feet to 400 feet long."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
